### **Notebook Notes**

*   **Shell:** Text interface to control computer.
*   **Key Commands:**
    *   `pwd` - see current location
    *   `ls` - list contents
    *   `cd <dir>` - move into folder
    *   `cd ..` - move up one level
    *   `mkdir <name>` - make folder
    *   `touch <file>` - make file
    *   `rm <file>` - delete file
    *   `rm -rf <dir>` - **!!** delete folder & everything in it **!!**
*   **Warning:** The terminal is powerful. Deleting with `rm` is permanent (no recycle bin).

